00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:19.160
Almost an hour.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.300
We've got time to grab some food if you want.

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:23.100
Mm, yum, yum.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:46.310
What do you have?

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.630
The bone. Dressing on the side, please.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.960
I'll try the deep-fried candy canes.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:53.050
Uh, the small dead fish sampler.

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:55.610
Maybe I should have tried the reindeer chow.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:57.620
Here's the latest from the North Pole.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.980
Santa Claus has scheduled a press conference.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.220
for 11 o'clock tonight.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:03.520
He is expected to cancel his flight

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.940
for the first time ever.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.930
Hey, everybody.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.030
Don't despair.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:11.430
I'm Olive, and I'm going to the North Pole

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.270
to help Santa.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:13.990
I'm the other reindeer.

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:16.810
What's the matter?

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.490
Haven't you people ever seen

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.550
a small dog-like reindeer before?

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:21.690
Olive!

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:22.710
Olive!

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:23.960
Olive!

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:25.600
Olive!

00:17:26.990 --> 00:17:27.250
Olive!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:28.900
Okay.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:31.900
You're Olive, the other reindeer?

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:33.780
Santa's looking for you.

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:35.140
He's out in the parking lot.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.200
He wants to give you a flying test.

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.940
Oh, boy. My big moment.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.450
Wish me luck, guys.

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:43.030
Coming, Santa!

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:45.450
I think the word mislikes me.

00:17:49.990 --> 00:17:51.210
Santa couldn't make it.

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:54.070
But I'll let him know you failed the test.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:09.320
Neither rain nor snow, etc. will keep me from keeping you from the North Pole and saving Christmas!

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:21.880
It's beginning to look nothing like Christmas.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:25.370
Poison me shall go.

00:18:26.530 --> 00:18:28.170
I don't know if that's me.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:29.830
I'm a negative day.

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.780
Dear Santa, I hate you, and I hope you never come again.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.540
Stay home. Love, Bobby.

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:40.990
Hmm, that's strange.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.110
Hey, don't tamper with the mail.

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.040
It's a federal offense.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.840
But it's addressed to me.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:54.160
Oh, okay, then.

00:18:57.260 --> 00:18:58.660
Great for zoo monkeys.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:18:59.760
Hmm.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:29.980
Postal regulations require you to stay put and keep quiet postman wasn't it we found

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.160
I found the waitress clothes. How'd you get away?

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:36.810
Kind of hard to explain. Have you ever heard of Deus Ex Machina?

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:37.650
Denise who?

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:42.410
Look it up. But listen, we missed the bus. You should have gone on without me.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:44.100
Ah, spare me the modern.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:49.310
I just called the postal service to complain about that postman. Guess what? I got that voicemail.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:51.530
How can we get to the North Pole now?

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:58.400
That was the last bus. I take you up myself, Olive, but if I don't get back to the depot in time, I'll lose my job. I'm sorry.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:19:59.700
You could always sell watches.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:02.540
You might find someone in the bar who'll take you up.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.580
We'll try it.

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:05.680
Thanks, Richard, for everything.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.280
I'm rooting for you, Olive.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.500
You other reindeer.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.200
Merry Christmas and, uh, Happy Hanukkah.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.400
I'm Santa's replacement reindeer.

00:20:32.740 --> 00:20:34.200
I need a ride to the North Pole

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:36.280
so I can help pull the sleigh and save Christmas.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:38.880
Anyone?

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:41.990
You don't look like no reindeer to me, mutt.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.370
Well, I am, and my name's Olive.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:45.610
Can you fly?

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:46.620
Um.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:48.410
Oh, sure she can fly.

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:49.770
She can fly like a bird.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:51.940
Like the kind of birds that fly, I mean.

00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:52.840
Oh, really?

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:53.660
Let's see.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.730
Amazing, just what Santa needs.

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:04.830
It's a miracle. We found another flying reindeer, and Christmas is back on again.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:05.130
Oh!

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:08.100
Sorry, Arturo.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.200
Please, just let me.

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:14.460
Hey! Let's take her up to the roof and see how she flies.

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:25.230
That's enough, fellas. We'll just leave now. We don't want any trouble.

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:27.980
Oh-ho, it's Mr. Briefcase. Let's see what you got in there.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:35.190
Watch, pal! That's valuable merchandise! It's mine!

00:21:35.530 --> 00:21:37.590
Arf! Arf! Arf! Arf!

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:40.180
A barking reindeer. Isn't that just...

00:21:40.180 --> 00:21:41.320
Stow it, tundra breath!

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:44.860
Maybe I'm just a little runt with no antlers.

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:48.020
But it looks like I'm the only one who's trying to save Christmas.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.300
