00:33:31.420 --> 00:33:32.320
Excuse me.

00:33:37.660 --> 00:33:42.540
I got another present. I must have been extra bad this year.

00:33:43.610 --> 00:33:44.690
Mmm, let's see.

00:33:45.340 --> 00:33:47.540
Doll. Jack in the box.

00:33:47.800 --> 00:33:49.100
Uh, cordless drill.

00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:51.120
Aha! Here we go!

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:54.320
The train set that should have been mine when I was a kid.

00:33:54.600 --> 00:33:57.860
That was the year Santa started putting me on his naughty list.

00:33:58.040 --> 00:33:59.980
He didn't cut me any slack, so I'm-

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.520
I'm not cutting him any slack.

00:34:01.700 --> 00:34:03.480
Old fat boy's finished!

00:34:03.780 --> 00:34:04.280
Ha ha ha!

00:34:04.560 --> 00:34:05.500
Ho ho ho!

00:34:08.850 --> 00:34:19.600
At the first house and I'm beat.

00:34:20.050 --> 00:34:21.570
You want some lichen-flavored gum?

00:34:21.770 --> 00:34:22.690
It'll perk you up.

00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:24.340
What's this?

00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:26.000
Credit card offers?

00:34:26.670 --> 00:34:27.230
Catalogs?

00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:28.910
Sweep sticks mailings?

00:34:29.540 --> 00:34:29.860
Bad!

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:39.210
News gang somehow we got the wrong sack. This is all junk mail. What's that? Let me smell that mail

00:34:41.570 --> 00:34:49.360
The postman I knew it. Let's go, but where just head north sooner or later. I'll pick up the scent

00:34:50.760 --> 00:34:58.630
It's getting awfully late

00:35:01.120 --> 00:35:01.600
This way!

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:33.400
Martini, too? Oh, now you're in for it.

00:35:35.420 --> 00:35:37.500
That's it. A little over.

00:35:39.530 --> 00:35:40.970
Oh, no, you don't!

00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:46.610
Get off me, you jolly old busybody!

00:36:01.950 --> 00:36:02.190
Go!

00:36:32.380 --> 00:36:48.920
Was that you or your stunt double?

00:36:49.160 --> 00:36:51.700
Oh, go on! Are you okay, Martini?

00:36:54.400 --> 00:36:55.960
Shaken, but not stirred.

00:36:56.280 --> 00:36:58.180
Anyway, all the toys are here!

00:36:58.490 --> 00:36:59.970
Also, a cordless...

00:37:02.360 --> 00:37:04.320
Thanks for your help, Martini.

00:37:05.280 --> 00:37:07.200
I'd offer you a lift in the sleigh,

00:37:07.240 --> 00:37:08.620
but Comet says no hitchhikers.

00:37:09.420 --> 00:37:11.100
Just our luck that you're flightless.

00:37:11.360 --> 00:37:12.540
Hey, don't worry about me.

00:37:12.830 --> 00:37:13.550
I'll drive home.

00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:14.860
I mean, how hard can it be?

00:37:15.140 --> 00:37:17.220
Plus, someone's got to take care of Mr. Zip.

00:37:20.540 --> 00:37:24.230
Ooh, bored wing.

00:37:25.850 --> 00:37:27.370
Time to go ho-ho!

00:37:31.020 --> 00:37:33.680
Thanks for everything, Martini. What will you do now?

00:37:34.290 --> 00:37:37.610
Eh, you know, I'll do a little loan sharking, sell a little lamb weight.

00:37:37.950 --> 00:37:40.370
Don't worry about me. Merry Christmas, Olive.

00:37:40.650 --> 00:37:42.090
Merry Christmas, Martini.

00:37:42.330 --> 00:37:42.530
Aw.

00:37:47.930 --> 00:37:52.780
Olive, great job getting the toys back, but we're way behind schedule.

00:37:53.240 --> 00:37:55.840
Any chance we could go faster, gang?

00:37:56.250 --> 00:37:57.760
Warp speed, Captain!

00:37:58.160 --> 00:37:58.920
Ho, ho!

00:38:11.000 --> 00:38:14.580
No clue, but now I've got the reindeer move.

00:38:15.850 --> 00:38:16.310
True blue.

00:38:18.380 --> 00:38:20.980
Good to call it to remind us.

00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:23.500
Can't give up on Christmas Eve.

00:38:24.440 --> 00:38:26.900
The trouble's all behind us.

00:38:27.340 --> 00:38:28.830
It's all a dark belief.

00:38:40.880 --> 00:38:41.220
It's crazy.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.490
Strings to fly Christmas Day

00:39:03.220 --> 00:39:06.100
So that all is to remind you

00:39:06.100 --> 00:39:08.520
On Christmas Eve

00:39:08.520 --> 00:39:11.970
It's all right inside you

00:39:11.970 --> 00:39:26.240
It's all Christmas

00:39:26.240 --> 00:39:26.700
Help

00:39:30.960 --> 00:39:33.160
To all the creatures, brave and small

00:39:33.160 --> 00:39:36.150
Will you stay, they have a ball

00:39:36.150 --> 00:39:37.760
So Merry Christmas

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:11.650
Guess I could deliver this stuff. It's not as glamorous as helping Santa, but there'll be trouble if the folks can't enter their sweepstakes

00:40:11.770 --> 00:40:17.090
Besides Christmas gratuities. That's it. All done

00:40:17.460 --> 00:40:23.220
Excellent work boys and three cheers for Olive the other reindeer

00:40:27.820 --> 00:40:29.660
After we get home and relax for a while

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:31.580
We usually go out for some reindeer games.

00:40:31.910 --> 00:40:32.630
Will you join us?

00:40:33.910 --> 00:40:34.470
Maybe.

00:40:35.540 --> 00:40:37.540
Hey! It's my house!

00:40:39.040 --> 00:40:40.810
Ido and Tim.

00:40:41.710 --> 00:40:42.750
Well, think about it.

00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:47.240
Oh, no. That arctic fog.

00:40:49.400 --> 00:40:52.260
Olive, I'm sorry, but we're lost in the fog.

00:40:52.440 --> 00:40:53.960
Could you smell us home?

00:40:54.480 --> 00:40:56.420
Mrs. Claus is baking cookies.

00:40:56.760 --> 00:40:57.260
Cookies?

00:41:00.540 --> 00:41:03.080
Gingerbread, 10 Degrees Starbird.

00:41:03.540 --> 00:41:22.960
Well, if I'd be honored if you'd call me Comet, the other dog.

00:41:23.420 --> 00:41:25.950
Sure, but first, geese.

00:41:30.700 --> 00:41:33.850
Well, I gotta hand it to you, Olive. You saved Christmas.

00:41:34.150 --> 00:41:37.540
No, I only convinced everyone else to do their best.

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:41.750
Oh, don't you be so modest, Olive. You were great.

00:41:42.050 --> 00:41:44.310
And now, ho, ho, ho!

00:41:44.750 --> 00:41:47.250
Presents for the staff and crew.

00:41:48.020 --> 00:41:48.160
Oh!

00:41:50.660 --> 00:41:54.360
Uh, boss, from an insurance point of view,

00:41:54.520 --> 00:41:56.780
the jump ropes, probably not a wise idea.

00:41:57.700 --> 00:41:59.970
Olive, here's something for you.

00:42:03.610 --> 00:42:05.310
Thank you.

00:42:07.530 --> 00:42:09.790
I know I'm not really a reindeer,

00:42:10.190 --> 00:42:11.970
but I'm proud I could help anyway.

00:42:12.630 --> 00:42:14.130
You've all been so wonderful.

00:42:14.880 --> 00:42:17.940
I'd love to stay, but I really must go home.

00:42:18.380 --> 00:42:19.300
I thought so.

00:42:19.650 --> 00:42:21.810
Let me finish my cappuccino and I'll give you a lift.

00:42:25.040 --> 00:42:27.080
Bye, Olive! Bye! We'll miss you!

00:42:27.160 --> 00:42:28.760
And Christmas, Olive!

00:42:31.820 --> 00:42:32.420
Merry Christmas!

00:42:38.020 --> 00:42:38.820
It's Martini!

00:42:39.670 --> 00:42:40.150
Martini!

00:42:40.480 --> 00:42:41.760
You helped save Christmas!

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:43.180
We saw you on TV!

00:42:43.620 --> 00:42:45.500
Oh, well, I hope it was a color set.

00:42:45.890 --> 00:42:47.370
Black and white doesn't do me justice.

00:42:48.240 --> 00:42:50.680
I'm pleased to offer you your old position back, Martini.

00:42:50.920 --> 00:42:55.320
The zoo can always find room for an extraordinary flightless aquatic bird who attracts media attention.

00:42:55.580 --> 00:42:58.810
And we've been a little short-handed since the monkeys escaped.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:03.120
Well, it's tempting, but I think I can get you an even better penguin.

00:43:18.380 --> 00:43:22.600
All of the other reindeer says Christmas? Huh?

00:43:25.100 --> 00:43:27.960
Merry Christmas, Tim. I hope you're not too mad at me.

00:43:28.320 --> 00:43:29.920
Olive! I was so worried.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:34.700
you'd never come back I'm sorry I was so mean can you ever forgive me I was so

00:43:34.700 --> 00:43:39.710
upset about Santa that I forgot I have the best dog in the whole world Wow and

00:43:39.710 --> 00:43:47.070
the best reindeer too Merry Christmas Olive good girl good girl
